KNOWNBUG
partial-assignment-before-non-constant-index2.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 \$past\(main\.i\) == 0 -> main\.a\[1\] == 7\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The assignment to a[i] is rewritten into an assignment to the whole of
a, using the value of a before the assignment. That value is taken to
be the current-state value of a whenever no single recorded slice
covers all of a, and hence the preceding blocking assignment to a[1]
is lost.
